# Copy to apps/web/.env and fill in. .env is git-ignored; nothing in this file is a secret.
#
# The map tile token. Without it the dispatch board draws the schematic — the same zones, visits and
# nurses, in their real positions, from the same contract, with no streets behind them and no
# network call at all. That is a supported state, not a broken one: every test in this repository
# runs without a token, and a build that ships without one still works.
#
# With a token the base map is Mapbox GL. Use a PUBLIC token (it begins pk.) — a public token is
# designed to be served to a browser. Never put a secret token (sk.) here; it would end up in the
# JavaScript bundle.
#
# Before using one in production, at account.mapbox.com:
#   1. Create a token scoped to MyThuso rather than reusing one from another project. A token shared
#      between products cannot be revoked for one of them.
#   2. Restrict it by URL to https://mythuso.co.za/* and https://www.mythuso.co.za/*, so a copy
#      lifted out of the bundle is worth nothing anywhere else.
#   3. Give it styles:read and fonts:read. It needs nothing else.
#
# The tile server is asked for streets and is told nothing about the caseload: no visit, no patient
# and no nurse position is ever sent to a mapping provider. See packages/catalog/geography.json.
VITE_MAPBOX_TOKEN=""
